  "published": "2026-08-13T04:30:34.94Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.0 adds FSST16 (2-byte codes, up to 65,535 symbols, symbols up to 16 bytes) — the variant the Parquet FSST proposal calls FSST_16.\n\nBreaking:\n- TryDecompress now returns false for malformed input as well as a too-small destination, where it previously decoded as much as it could. The new Decompress overload returns OperationStatus so the two are distinguishable, and the allocating overloads throw InvalidDataException on corruption.\n- FSST8 and FSST12 produce different compressed bytes, as a result of the ratio fixes below. Data written by earlier versions still decodes; no reader change is needed.\n\nFixes, all affecting compression ratio:\n- FSST8 length-2 symbols were in the table but unreachable when compressing.\n- Probe symbols carried a zeroed code field, making any symbol whose length matched the available input unreachable unless its code was 0 — every length-8 symbol, and every symbol at the end of a short value. Affected FSST8 and FSST12.\n- The pair-frequency counter overflowed past 3,840 occurrences into an adjacent pair's slot, inventing symbols absent from the input.\n\nMeasured on a synthetic URL corpus: FSST8 1.93x to 3.11x, FSST12 2.07x to 2.71x. Compression is 2.7-3.0x faster and FSST12 training 3.1x.",
